Contributing to Hydra
=====================


Building
--------

    make build       outputs bin/hydra
    make test        go test -count=1 ./...
    make vet         go vet ./...
    make fmt         gofmt + goimports


Code style
----------

  * gofmt is mandatory.  Run `make fmt` before committing.
  * Follow idiomatic Go: short names in local scope, descriptive
    names in package scope, interfaces defined by consumers, errors
    returned not thrown.
  * Comments: godoc on exported symbols.  Internal functions get a
    one-liner if the name doesn't tell the whole story.  Don't explain
    "why" in the code -- put that in a commit message.
  * No panic in library code.  No os.Exit outside cmd/hydra.
  * Prefer pointer fields (*int64) over Has*bool pairs for optional
    struct values.


Commit messages
---------------

Subject line: imperative mood, lowercase, no period.

    fix failover loop skipping healthy accounts

    When all accounts had location errors, the retry logic reset the
    tried map but didn't reset locationFailures, causing the next
    iteration to skip the retry path entirely.

Reference the issue if applicable.  Keep the body under 72 columns.


Pull requests
-------------

  * One logical change per PR.
  * Run `make test vet fmt-check` before pushing.
  * If adding a new endpoint, add a test in *_test.go.
  * If changing the config schema, update config.example.toml and the
    README configuration section.


Project structure
-----------------

    cmd/hydra/          entry point
    internal/
      account/          OAuth, account store, quota, request logging
      app/              service layer (CLI/TUI -> store interfaces)
      cli/              cobra commands, TUI, output rendering
      config/           TOML config + env var overrides
      db/               SQLite wrapper + migrations
      proxy/            HTTP handlers, SSE streaming, failover, health
    Makefile            build / install / test / vet / fmt
